-- Momo v3.52 — Support recommendation to split overloaded Knowledge entries
-- Run in Supabase SQL Editor, then reindex Momo Support documentation from
-- Admin > Support > Knowledge Base > Reindexar documentação.
-- No schema changes are required.

update public.knowledge_entries
set
  content = 'Momo Support can help an authenticated client prepare wording before a manual Knowledge Base entry is saved. The client can paste raw business information into Support. Support may rewrite only for clarity, structure and self-contained wording; it must preserve every supplied fact, condition, exception, limitation, name, price, amount, date, duration, unit, location and policy, and it must not invent or silently remove information. If the source is ambiguous, contradictory or missing context needed for a reliable statement, Support asks a concise clarifying question before producing the final draft. Good Knowledge Base wording is factual, direct, self-contained and focused on one coherent topic. Support must actively check whether the raw material contains multiple independently answerable topics, policies, conditions or restrictions that a visitor could reasonably ask about separately. When it does, Support should recommend splitting the material into separate Knowledge entries, briefly explain why, and propose a clear title/category/topic for each entry before anything is saved. Text should not be split just because it is long: conditions and exceptions needed to understand the same policy should remain together. When a split is recommended, every supplied fact must be accounted for across the proposed entries without changing meaning, silently dropping information or duplicating meaning unnecessarily. Examples that normally benefit from splitting include accepted reference types versus a separate policy on copying another artist, opening hours versus returns policy, and shipping rules versus payment rules. The automatic Support save flow handles one entry at a time, so a multi-entry split is proposed first and the client chooses which entry to prepare; Support must not mark a multi-entry proposal as a final save-ready draft. When one final draft is ready, Support shows the exact Title, Category and Content for review. The Portal then shows Add to Knowledge and I want to edit chat actions. Only an authenticated Owner can use Add to Knowledge; the button is the explicit save confirmation and creates the entry as Public + Published with its embedding immediately. A normal text message does not save the draft. If the client requests a correction, Support revises and shows the complete draft again before the save action is used. Members can prepare and review drafts but cannot save Knowledge Base changes. The automatic Support save flow does not currently create Internal or Draft entries; those visibility/status choices remain available through Portal > Knowledge Base.',
  embedding = null,
  updated_at = now()
where agent_key = 'momo-support'
  and slug = 'momo-support-knowledge-drafting';
